 "text": "Hi, how have you been? Of course. Gluten free dinner means there are plenty of treatments for the restaurant owner. Pasta, of course, is out. So are most sandwich breads. You' notice they don't have gluten free sign. Most gluten free guests are there because of a diagnosis, and restaurants don't want to frighten them away. Pasta and bread are out, so no pasta and no bread. Pasta pasta and bread bread are fine. Then ask if you can use it on pasta, or get a sauce without it. Pasta and sauce are okay. And think of alternative bread like crisps or toast. It is, but there are plenty of alternatives. Ask about sauces and alternative bread. Your roommate can still enjoy sushi, she'll just use rice instead of rice and no bread.",
